About Bosch Engineering Center Cluj
 Since its establishment in 2013, Bosch Engineering Center Cluj plays an essential role in the current transformation of the mobility sector. Through its extensive expertise in software, hardware & mechanical engineering, reliability engineering, as well as sales planning, the center contributes to the development of innovative products and services based on artificial intelligence (AI) applied in the fields of automated driving, electric and connected mobility. Thanks to the diverse professional and personal development opportunities, flexible working conditions, modern offices and laboratories in Cluj-Napoca, Jucu, Bucharest and Sibiu, we are one of the most desired employers among engineers and IT professionals in Romania.
 Our promise to our colleagues is rock-solid: we grow together, we enjoy our work, and inspire each other. Join us and see the difference.
 Work LikeABosch
 Job Description
 We are looking for an Embedded Software Engineer to develop and deliver advanced driver assistance functions for next-generation vehicles. In this role, you will transform system requirements into vehicle control functionalities, ensuring safety, performance, and driver comfort.
 Key Responsibilities:
Define the software design for ADAS driving functions;
Develop and maintain embedded software for;
Longitudinal control functions;
Lateral control functions;
Driver assistance and intervention strategies;
Safety and comfort feature implementation;
Design and implement control logic in C/C++ for automotive embedded systems;
Drive requirements analysis, implementation, reviews, and traceability;
Support vehicle testing, calibration, and performance optimization;
Develop engineering tools and automation scripts using Python;
Analyze vehicle measurements and system behavior using Vector toolchain;
Collaborate closely with system architects, vehicle dynamics, and safety teams;
Support software verification, validation, and integration activities;
Contribute to continuous improvement of software development processes and methodologies.
 Qualifications
Strong proficiency in C/C++ development for embedded systems;
Experience with ADAS systems is a plus;
Understanding of longitudinal and lateral vehicle dynamics;
Good understanding of software development processes;
Experience with Python scripting and automation;
Familiarity with Git, DOORS, and Vector tools;
Knowledge of software architecture and real-time systems;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills;
Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to document architecture, APIs and integration guidelines.
